--- body ---
## Context

Found by the ticket 0343 wrap-up sweep. `.claude/skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`
step 5 says "Credentials from `.env`: `HAL_ID`, `HAL_PASSWORD`". Neither is in
`.env`, and neither has been — 0343 removed `AGENT_GH_TOKEN`, `OPENALEX_API_KEY`
and `S2_API_KEY`, never these. So this predates 0343 and was not caused by it;
0343 only made the class visible.

Both values *do* exist in `~/.config/keys/hal.env`. What is missing is the
selection: the `KEYS=` line in `.env` does not name `hal`, and selection is
default-deny, so nothing loads them. Measured from the repo root with the loader
active — `HAL_ID: ABSENT`, `HAL_PASSWORD: ABSENT`.

Consequence: the HAL SWORD deposit step of `/update-publist` cannot authenticate.
The failure mode matches the one 0343 documented — a missing credential reads as
an ordinary auth failure rather than as misconfiguration, so the cause is not
obvious from the error.

## Scope change (author decision, 2026-07-27)

`update-publist` is a **harness** skill (`~/.claude/skills/update-publist/`).
The project copy was a stale fork that shadowed it — two different documents
disagreeing on fact (the fork puts `Ha-Duong.bib` at `~/CNRS/html/`, the harness
copy at `src/`; only the harness copy has the payload-review gate and the
credential-safety rules). Both carried the same stale credential-source claim,
in different words.

Repairing the fork would have kept two documents alive. The author chose to
delete it, so this repo's half of the work is the *selection* only:

- delete `.claude/skills/update-publist/` and its two references in `AGENTS.md`;
- keep the `KEYS=` extension in `.env` (a `/update-publist` run started from this
  repo root reads *this* `.env` — the loader keys off the shell's startup PWD);
- keep the `STALE_ENV_CLAIMS` ratchet, pinning **both** phrasings so neither
  document's wording can be pasted back in;
- keep the HAL names in `REQUIRED_KEYS_EXPORTS`.

That last bullet reverses a call made when this scope change was drafted. The
reasoning then was "no code in this tree reads them, so the list should not name
them" — the list meaning "this project's code breaks without it". Review
falsified the premise. `bash-env.sh` exports every project-`.env` key verbatim,
`KEYS` included, so a project `KEYS=` line **replaces** the harness one instead
of adding to it. Measured from a directory whose `.env` selects only `openalex`:
`HAL_ID` unset, despite `~/.claude/.env` selecting `hal`. So the selection in
*this* `.env` is the only one a deposit launched from this repo ever sees, and
dropping it would leave every test green and the deposit broken — precisely the
silent failure this ticket exists to close. The list's meaning widens to
"credentials that must resolve for work started in this repo".

Two things landed outside this PR: `~/.claude/.env` gained the same `hal`
selection (machine-local, no value written) so the skill authenticates from any
cwd, and the harness repo gets its own PR for the stale line in its `SKILL.md`.

## Relevant files

- `.env` — the `KEYS=` line needs a `hal` selection. Gitignored, machine-local,
  and **never** a place to write the values themselves.
- `~/.config/keys/hal.env` — already holds `HAL_ID` and `HAL_PASSWORD`, mode 0600.
- `.claude/skills/update-publist/` — the shadowing fork, deleted.
- `AGENTS.md` — two references to the deleted fork.
- `tests/test_env_has_no_secret_literals.py` — `REQUIRED_KEYS_EXPORTS` and
  `STALE_ENV_CLAIMS` are the two ratchets that cover this.

## Actions

1. Extend the `KEYS=` line with `hal:HAL_ID,hal:HAL_PASSWORD` (selection form,
   not bare `hal` — same least-privilege reasoning as the other four).
2. Delete `.claude/skills/update-publist/` and drop it from `AGENTS.md`.
3. Pin both stale phrasings in `STALE_ENV_CLAIMS`.
4. Add both names to `REQUIRED_KEYS_EXPORTS` so dropping the selection fails a
   test rather than a deposit.
5. Extend `~/.claude/.env` with the same selection (outside the repo).
6. Correct the credential-source line in the harness `SKILL.md`, and port the
   four sections only the deleted fork carried (separate PR).

## Test

Two ratchets in `tests/test_env_has_no_secret_literals.py`:
`test_keys_line_selects_every_consumed_credential` fails if either selection is
dropped from `KEYS=`; `test_no_doc_claims_env_supplies_credentials` fails if
either stale phrasing returns to a tracked file. Names only in any assertion
message — never a value.

## Verification

- [x] `HAL_ID` and `HAL_PASSWORD` resolve from the repo root and from a worktree
- [x] Each matches `~/.config/keys/hal.env` **by hash** — never by printing
- [x] They also resolve from a cwd outside the project (harness-level selection)
- [x] Dropping either from `KEYS=` fails a test — measured against a `.env`
      selecting only `openalex`: both names unset, harness selection overridden
- [x] No tracked file names `.env` as the source of a credential
- [ ] The harness `SKILL.md` no longer does either — harness PR #680, open

## Invariants

- No credential value in any committed file, test output, or PR description.
- `~/.config/keys/` stays the single store; do not copy values into `.env`.
- No CI (AGENTS.md, ticket 0321): run `make check` locally before the PR.

## Exit criteria

`/update-publist` can authenticate to HAL because `KEYS=` selects both
credentials from the keystore, one surviving skill document names that source
correctly, and a test fails if either the selection is dropped or the
"credentials from `.env`" claim returns.
